<h2>Status Icons Explained</h2>
<p>The table below explains the status icons used in the table above. The status icons indicate whether the LEI issuing organization uploaded files in time for inclusion in the latest relevant Concatenated File based on the applicable <span><a href="https://www.gleif.org/en/about-lei/common-data-file-format">Common Data File (CDF) format</a></span>:  LEI-CDF format version 3.1 (LEI-CDF v3.1), Relationship Record CDF format version 2.1 (RR-CDF v2.1); Reporting Exceptions format version 2.1.</p>
<table>
    <tr>
        <th></th>
        <th></th>
    </tr>
        <tr>
        <td class="source-file-status">
            <i class="fa fa-check" style="color: #51DAC5"></i>
        </td>
        <td>
            The source file was uploaded by the LEI issuing organization in time for the latest concatenation.        </td>
    </tr>
        <tr>
        <td class="source-file-status">
            <i class="fa fa-exclamation-circle yellow"></i>
        </td>
        <td>
            The source file was not uploaded by the LEI issuing organization in time for the latest concatenation. An earlier file was used to create the relevant GLEIF Concatenated File.        </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td class="source-file-status">
            <i class="fa fa-times-circle red"></i>
        </td>
        <td>
            No source file was uploaded to date by the LEI issuing organization. The relevant GLEIF Concatenated File does not contain data related to the LEIs managed by this LEI issuing organization.        </td>
    </tr>
</table>
